Package: synthplacebo
Title: Placebo-Calibrated Inference for the Demeaned Synthetic Control
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
 person("Jeffrey", "Milliman", email = "jeffmilliman2@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
 person("Claude", role = "ctb", comment = "AI model by Anthropic; wrote the code at the direction of Jeffrey Milliman"))
Description: Synthetic control for a single treated unit with placebo-calibrated inference. The demeaned
 synthetic control (an intercept plus non-negative donor weights that sum to one) is fitted to the treated
 unit's pre-treatment outcomes, and pointwise intervals, simultaneous bands and prediction intervals are
 calibrated against placebo fits of the donors. Includes time-varying covariate adjustment, ridge
 augmentation, diagnostics for treated units beyond the donors' range, the leave-two-out placebo test of
 Lei and Sudijono (2025) <arXiv:2401.07152> for small donor pools, power analysis, and a screen for
 covariates that break from their synthetic controls after treatment.
